<Base title="Advertise & Post — Transit411">
  <div class="page">
    <h1 class="disp">Advertise &amp; Post</h1>
    <p class="lede">Reach the people who move transit capital projects — agency staff, consultants, contractors, and program leaders.</p>
    <p>Transit411's audience is the professional core of the industry: the people responsible for funding, procuring, and delivering transit projects. If you're hiring, seeking bids, or want to put your firm in front of that audience, here's how.</p>

    <h2 class="disp">Ways to reach the audience</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Job postings</strong> — list a transit role (program management, engineering, planning, executive) where the right candidates are already reading.</li>
      <li><strong>Procurement &amp; solicitation postings</strong> — put an RFP, RFQ, or IFB in front of qualified firms.</li>
      <li><strong>Featured People</strong> — highlight a hire, promotion, or leadership move as a sponsored placement in the People section.</li>
      <li><strong>Newsletter sponsorship</strong> — sponsor the Transit411 Intelligence email.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="disp">Get started</h2>
    <p>Postings and sponsorships are handled directly for now. Email <a href="mailto:advertise@transit411.net">advertise@transit411.net</a> with what you'd like to post or promote, and we'll send current options and rates.</p>
    <p class="meta">Self-serve posting and pricing are coming as the marketplace launches.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
